# Object Property: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> (denoted by family)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> "Intentially not a sub-property of \"denoted by\" as this rescticts using \"denoted by\" in property chains of its sub-properties")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> "The sub-properties are inferrable through corresponding property chains")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> "denoted by family"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> "denoted by family is a top-level object property between a crystallographic entity, i.e., plane or direction, and the family of Miller indices"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> "Consider a (011) crystallographic plane in cubic lattice, i.e., the instance of the plane is denoted by (011) instance. The instance of the plane is be inferred to be of type \"crystallographic entity in cubic system\" and carries \"is cubic\" reftexive triple. The (011) is a member of {110} family of Miller indices. The property chain \"is cubic + denoted by + member of\" will infer that the plane is denoted by {110} in a cubic lattice."@en)
SubObjectPropertyOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> owl:topObjectProperty)
ObjectPropertyRange(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164> ObjectUnionOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000021> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000023>))

# Object Property: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000168> (denoted by family under cubic symmetry)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000168> "denoted by family under cubic symmetry")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000168> "denoted by family under cubic symmetry is an object property between a crystallographic entity in cubic system, i.e., plane or direction, and the family of Miller indices."@en)
SubObjectPropertyOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000168> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000164>)
ObjectPropertyDomain(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000168> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000041>)

# Object Property: <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000170> (is cubic)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000170> "is cubic")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000170> "is cubic is a object property  for the inference of family of directions/planes Miller indices notation. The class crystallographic entity in cubic  system carries a Self restriction \"is cubic\""@en)
SubObjectPropertyOf(<https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000170> <https://w3id.org/pmd/cryo/CRYO_0000053>)


